      "updated_at": "2026-10-09T06:13:13Z",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "Concept ACK. All 7 cases in `bip-0054/test_vectors/coinbases.json` start from the mainnet genesis block. Its coinbase has `nLockTime` 0 and `nSequence` 0xffffffff, so the rule as written makes all of them invalid. bitcoin/bitcoin#35793 also skips the check at height 0.\n\nThe timewarp rule has the same gap: at N=0 there is no T<sub>N−1</sub>, and `timestamps.json` also starts from genesis. One sentence could exempt genesis from both rules.\n",
