        "type": "User",
        "site_admin": false,
        "name": null,
        "patch_url": null
      },
      "body": "This change seems incorrect and redundant to me. In technical writing, usually specific rules beat general rules. So, the proposed phrasing implies that all blocks except the Genesis block would have to follow this rule. However, such a rule would cause the entire blockchain after the Genesis block to be invalid. \r\n\r\nThe specification section starts with “For all blocks **after activation** the following new rules apply” (emphasis added), which is the accurate range of blocks for which this rule applies. Obviously, the soft fork cannot activate before or on the Genesis block in mainnet, and testnet5, is also proposed to activate the rules on block 1 rather than applying it for the Genesis block.\r\n\r\nSo, this rephrasing seems like a disimprovement to me.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-16T01:15:36Z",
